course: dictionary
lesson: 2768
title: Words that show feelings and rules
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Discouraged» means you have lost hope or confidence, so you do not want to keep trying. When a friend says, «Don't get discouraged!», they are telling you not to give up hope after a mistake.
explain: Discouraged is also the past form of discourage, which means to try to stop someone from doing something. Look for clues in the words after it. In «discouraged from doing», the sentence tells you what was being stopped.
explain: Some rules use discouraged too. «Welsh, once discouraged in schools, is now taught in every school in Wales.» Here discouraged means not approved of, so the schools did not support the language. Swap in your meaning and check that the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Discouraged can describe a feeling: you have lost hope or confidence.
fact: Discouraged is the past form of the verb discourage, which means to try to stop someone from doing something.
fact: Discouraged can also mean not approved of, as in «Phones are discouraged in class».
fact: The words around discouraged, such as «from» or «in class», give you clues to its meaning.
exercise: «Don't get discouraged!» What does discouraged mean here? | * Losing hope and no longer wanting to try | Wildly excited about trying again | Very tired after a long sleep | Lost in the woods
exercise: «Phones are discouraged in class.» What does discouraged mean here? | Given as a prize | Banned by the police | * Not approved of | Very loud
exercise: Mum discouraged me from climbing the wall. What did Mum do? | Helped me climb higher | Cheered me on loudly | Took a photo of me | * Tried to stop me
test: «Welsh, once discouraged in schools, is now taught in every school in Wales.» What does discouraged mean in this sentence? | Made into a song | Painted bright red | * Not approved of | Taught with great joy
test: After three losses, Ben felt discouraged. What does this tell you about Ben? | * He had lost hope and confidence | He was full of hope | He was very hungry | He had just won the match
exam: «The coach discouraged him from quitting.» What does discouraged mean in this sentence? | * Tried to stop him from quitting | Helped him to quit | Made him laugh about quitting | Gave him a prize for quitting
